# SFT execution status v0.103

2026-09-22. The approved one-shot sharded SDK diagnostic has completed. Its
workflow succeeded in reporting a per-shard limit; **the full SDK census and
capacity recovery did not complete**. No SDK deletion, setup probe, model/data
access, GPU, qualification or training occurred.

## Published and tested

Commit `c3cba987b2191ebfff1913a4a69ff05afe852daa` adds exactly four files and has
parent `7da33c657497386dc0e5cf4c6fb1f66bf03cfc05`. The script counts every shard
root (directory, regular file or symlink) as well as descendants. Re-listing
already counted entries does not spend the remaining node allowance again.
Only directories are opened inside the SDK; symlink targets and file contents
are never opened. The fixed target is `/usr/local/lib/android/sdk` on the fresh
GitHub VM, never the Mac.

There are 46 new tests and 126 frozen regressions: 172 combined tests pass on
both CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7. Ruff 0.15.1 and YAML checks pass. Independent
scope review found no blocking issue under the trusted disposable-VM premise.
Nineteen prior bound source/evidence hashes and the source-CI routing bindings
were verified unchanged.

Bounds were 250,000 accepted nodes per immediate-child shard (including its
root), 1,000,000 aggregate accepted nodes, directory depth below 48, 32 MiB
relative-name accounting per shard / 128 MiB aggregate, 64 GiB allocated blocks
per shard and aggregate, and a 240-second inner deadline. Accepted-node counts
are not total metadata syscall counts; re-list and identity checks repeat.
No cap was changed after the run started, and no retry occurred.

## Verified actual result

[Run 35687186159](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/35687186159),
attempt 1, job `106616411256`, ran from 04:31:09Z to 04:31:32Z (23 seconds).
All workflow steps succeeded. The report is an observed `budget_hit`, not a
complete census:

- 10 shards completed; shard 11 stopped at the 250,001st attempted node.
- 308,008 nodes were accepted in total, including 250,000 in the incomplete shard.
- The 1,000,000-node aggregate ceiling was not reached.
- Allocated-block accounting was 11,749,097,472 bytes in total, including
  2,789,654,528 bytes in the incomplete shard.
- Derived completed-shard totals: 58,008 nodes and 8,959,442,944 allocated bytes
  (about 8.34 GiB). These are not guaranteed physically reclaimable bytes.
- All SDK mutation, payload-read, setup, model/data, GPU, training and
  production-eligibility flags remain false.

The exact artifact `10676603939` is a 621-byte ZIP with server SHA-256
`c036321e3b1aff1daa45fa8c3a6bedb9ed87afe46e15ab407157759781401ff6`.
Only its single 889-byte canonical aggregate is retained. Aggregate SHA-256:
`1b83af8c0efcbf878b7da98beef5df2e6f0add5500000a99943fda1bdbb4cee7`.
Two offline verification passes checked the report schema, exact hashes, plan
bindings, result cross-bindings and derived totals. No raw job logs were fetched.

This proves that one immediate-child shard exceeded the per-shard bound on this
fresh image. It does not identify retained child names, prove the old run's
historical cause, or determine total SDK size. Sharding at this level did not
make a full-SDK cleanup ready. Gate 5 remains incomplete.

## Concrete next option, not executed

A separately approved partial cleanup could avoid raising the 250,000-node cap:
select **at most the first 10 immediate SDK children in deterministic sorted
order on a fresh VM**, fully census all selected shards before any deletion,
bind their current identities, and delete only those selected targets. Leave
all other SDK entries and the SDK root itself untouched. Stop before deletion
if any selected shard violates a bound or identity/mount check. After deletion,
measure actual free space and call setup only if the unchanged capacity floor
passes; otherwise stop without expanding targets.

This would be a new destructive authorization, not a continuation or retry of
the diagnostic. Provider images can change, so these cannot be described as
the same ten historical shards. Historical aggregate bytes must never replace
fresh admission checks or actual free-space measurement. No such cleanup,
successor implementation, workflow, cap increase or image acquisition has been
started in this turn.

All three workflows are now confirmed successful: this diagnostic, Spark
`35687186097`, and Source `35687186060` (all four Source jobs passed; last job
completed at 04:41:04Z). The remote branch tip remains the published commit.
This CI success is not a full SDK census, capacity acceptance or Gate 5 pass.

Local post-run receipts are the sharded aggregate and the matching result,
verification and CI-result files under `evidence/`. They are not pushed. Exact
automatic Source/Spark conclusions are recorded in
`lumi-4b-sft-sdk-sharded-census-ci-result-v0.1.json`. No post-run push or extra
execution was performed.
